---
description: "Audit the {{.Store}} (or a single project) for catalog hygiene: orphans, broken links, untagged docs, stale index entries, hub and document shape, ADR gaps. Read-only."
argument-hint: "[project-slug | blank = whole {{.Store}}] [--deep]"
---

Read-only health check over the project's {{.Store}}: one `mark_doctor` call runs every check and returns the report. **Never writes.** An organizational knowledge system is `/knowledge-doctor`'s territory ({{.KnowledgePluginName}} plugin).

{{template "store.tmpl" .}}

## Run

`$ARGUMENTS`: an optional project slug and `--deep` (metadata lost across versions).

`mark_doctor` through the store's server: `url` is `/<slug>/` for one project, `/` for the whole {{.Store}} (a broker store: `mark://<world>/` from `mark_worlds`, then `/<slug>/` under it); `deep: true` with `--deep`. An invalid slug or scope is the tool's own refusal.{{if ne .Harness "cowork"}} Whole local {{.Store}}: also run `"$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" provision verify-auth` via Bash and relay its verdict as one line after the report; a non-zero exit is a coverage gap, not a finding.{{end}}

- Success: print the report verbatim, then a short prioritized "what I'd fix first". "All clean" only with zero findings, Coverage `complete`{{if ne .Harness "cowork"}} and a healthy verify-auth verdict where one was due{{end}}; otherwise name the gaps.
- Tool error (store unreachable, unauthorized, inventory bound, scope not found): surface it verbatim, stop. Never substitute a manual crawl.

## Don't

- Write or modify anything; a requested fix is a separate, explicit step.
- Fabricate findings or coverage the report does not state.
